.\" robodr-metrics(1). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-ops/src/bin/robodr-metrics.rs and the module docs of
.\" crates/robodr-ops/src/metrics.rs. Keep them in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-METRICS 1 "2026-10-31" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-metrics \- Prometheus textfile exporter of RoboDR's status files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-metrics
.RB [ \-\-agentd\-status
.I FILE
|
.BR \-\-no\-agentd ]
.RB [ \-\-uplink\-status
.I FILE
|
.BR \-\-no\-uplink ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-units ]
.RB [ \-\-out
.I FILE
|
.BR \-\-stdout ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Renders
.BR robodr\-agentd (8)'s
.I status.json
and
.BR robodr\-uplink (1)'s
.I uplink\-status.json
and the systemd state of RoboDR's services
.RB ( "systemctl show" )
in the Prometheus text exposition format, for node_exporter's textfile
collector. RoboDR opens no port for monitoring: the scraper sees only the
file. The file holds counters and states; no finding content, error text,
batch id or health reason is exported, and the only label values are the
robot id, the profile and safety states, input names, the uplink state
(one of five fixed values) and RoboDR's own unit names, escaped.
.PP
Freshness is judged exactly as agentd defines it: running, written on this
boot, younger than its
.B stale_after_ms
by
.BR CLOCK_MONOTONIC .
A stopped, hung or previous-boot agent is
.B robodr_agentd_fresh 0
and
.BR robodr_agentd_state{state=\(dqunknown\(dq} " 1",
never a stale "ok". A missing or unreadable status file is
.BR "robodr_agentd_status_readable 0" ,
and the file is still written.
.SH METRICS
.TP
.B robodr_metrics_last_run_timestamp_seconds
when the file was written; alert on its age to catch a stopped exporter.
.TP
.BR robodr_agentd_status_readable ", " robodr_agentd_running ", " robodr_agentd_fresh
0 or 1.
.TP
.BI robodr_agentd_state{state=} ok|degraded|unknown
one-hot effective monitoring state.
.TP
.BR robodr_agentd_status_age_seconds ", " robodr_agentd_uptime_seconds ", " robodr_agentd_health_reasons
.TP
.BR robodr_agentd_queue_bytes ", " robodr_agentd_queue_bytes_max ", " robodr_agentd_evidence_degraded ", " robodr_agentd_signs_findings
.TP
.B robodr_agentd_info{robot_id,profile_status,safety_state}
always 1.
.TP
.BI robodr_agentd_input_ FIELD {input}
per-input counters.
.TP
.BI robodr_agentd_ SECTION _ PATH
every numeric counter of the status sections
.BR daemon ", " agent ", " spool ", " pipeline ", " blackbox ,
.BR discovery_flood ", " correlation ", " control_plane ", " executor ,
.B safety_feed
(type
.BR untyped :
counters of the running process, reset on restart; use
.BR rate() / increase() ).
.TP
.BR robodr_uplink_status_readable ", " robodr_uplink_state{state}
uplink state
.RB ( ok ", " retrying ", " blocked ", " starting ;
any other value is
.BR other ).
.TP
.BR robodr_uplink_status_age_seconds ", " robodr_uplink_last_success_age_seconds ", " robodr_uplink_last_delivery_age_seconds ", " robodr_uplink_stuck_seconds
by the wall clock.
.TP
.BI robodr_uplink_ FIELD
its counters (backlog as
.BR robodr_uplink_backlog_* ;
times are not exported as counters).
.TP
.B robodr_units_readable
1 if systemd answered
.BR "systemctl show" .
.TP
.BR robodr_unit_active{unit} ", " robodr_unit_failed{unit}
0 or 1, for every RoboDR service systemd has loaded (installed and not
masked). A unit systemd gave up restarting is
.BR failed .
.TP
.B robodr_unit_enabled{unit}
1 if the unit's
.B UnitFileState
is
.B enabled
or
.BR enabled-runtime :
the site expects it to run. Enabled, not active and not failed is a unit
that is down without systemd calling it failed (for example a start job
that failed an
.BR Assert ...= ).
.TP
.B robodr_unit_restarts{unit}
systemd's
.B NRestarts
(automatic restarts since the unit was last started by hand): a crash
loop, or a daemon killed again and again at its
.BR MemoryMax= .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-agentd\-status " FILE"
default
.IR /var/lib/robodr/spool/agentd/status.json .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-agentd
no agentd metrics (a SOC relay).
.TP
.BI \-\-uplink\-status " FILE"
default
.IR /var/lib/robodr/export/uplink/uplink\-status.json ,
read only when it exists (an explicitly named file that is missing is
exported as unreadable).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-uplink
no uplink metrics.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-units
do not ask systemd for the unit states.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
absolute,
.IR *.prom ;
written atomically (temporary file, fsync, rename), mode 0644. Default
.IR /run/robodr\-metrics/robodr.prom .
.TP
.B \-\-stdout
print instead.
.SH SETUP
The package ships an example service and timer (every 15 s) and example
alert rules in
.IR /usr/share/doc/robodr/examples/metrics/ :
.PP
.nf
install \-m 0644 robodr\-metrics.service.example /etc/systemd/system/robodr\-metrics.service
install \-m 0644 robodr\-metrics.timer.example /etc/systemd/system/robodr\-metrics.timer
systemctl daemon\-reload && systemctl enable \-\-now robodr\-metrics.timer
.fi
.PP
Point node_exporter at the directory
.RB ( \-\-collector.textfile.directory=/run/robodr\-metrics )
or symlink
.I /run/robodr\-metrics/robodr.prom
into the directory it already reads. The example service runs with
.B CAP_DAC_READ_SEARCH
only (to read the 0600 uplink status), no network, a read-only OS, and the
key and evidence trees hidden. Load
.I robodr\-alerts.example.yml
into Prometheus and adjust the thresholds; every metric it names is checked
against the exporter's output in the test suite.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
written.
.TP
.B 1
the output could not be written.
.TP
.B 2
usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-agentd (8),
.BR robodr\-uplink (1),
.BR robodr\-support\-bundle (8)
